    instructions: "Whisk egg yolks and sugar over a double boiler until pale and thick, about 8 min. Remove from heat, fold in mascarpone. Whip cream to stiff peaks, fold into mascarpone mixture. Combine espresso and liqueur. Quickly dip each ladyfinger into espresso (do not soak). Layer half the ladyfingers in a 9×13 dish, spread half the cream, repeat. Refrigerate at least 6 hours. Dust with cocoa and chocolate shavings before serving."
