    instructions: "Cook spaghetti in salted boiling water until al dente. While pasta cooks, warm olive oil in a large skillet over low heat. Add garlic and red pepper flakes; cook until garlic is pale gold, about 3 min (do not brown). Reserve 1 cup pasta water, then drain spaghetti. Add spaghetti to skillet, toss vigorously, adding pasta water a splash at a time until silky. Remove from heat, fold in parsley. Top with Pecorino if desired."
